Cobalt Service Partners | Milwaukee, WI; Nashville, TN; or Atlanta, GA (On-site, about 50% travel) | Reports to: Director of Operations, Entrance Solutions &nbsp;

About Cobalt Service Partners

Cobalt is a private equity-backed platform building the leading commercial door and entrance business in the country. Entrance Solutions, Cobalt's door and entrance group, is six operating companies across the Southeast and Midwest, growing well above the industry and actively acquiring . Cobalt is backed by Alpine Investors, a private equity firm specializing in middle market companies in the services and software industries and with $15bn+ of AUM. Cobalt's Co-CEOs (Tyler Hoffman and Anthony Gonzalez) are experienced investors and operators. &nbsp;

Position overview &nbsp;

Cobalt's Entrance Solutions group is hiring an Operational Excellence Manager to join their growting operations team. The role takes proven operating standards (technician utilization , job readiness, job costing, and scorecard s ) and makes them stick inside every company in the group. &nbsp;

This is a hands-on role. Half the work is in the field with technicians, dispatchers, and branch leaders. The other half is building the models, data pulls, and integrations that make the numbers trustworthy and automatic. You'll have a meaningful role in creating our new operating standards, and have a hands-on opportunity to improve the end-to-end processes of our businesses. &nbsp;

What you will do &nbsp;

• Drive technician utilization up across the group, with clear visibility into where every hour goes. &nbsp;

• Roll out one operating model in every company: jobs ready before they're scheduled, common job costing, and a weekly scorecard. &nbsp;

• Work on-site inside partner companies, alongside technicians, dispatchers, and branch leaders, until new standards hold . &nbsp;

• Build the models, data pulls, and system integrations that make scorecard data accurate and automatic. &nbsp;

• Find where AI and automation save real hours, ship it, and measure the result. &nbsp;

• L ead service-side implementation projects across the group in 2027. &nbsp;

• Build a business case for every project and track its impact on the P&amp;L. &nbsp;

• Assist with our digital transformation and technology standardization across the portfolio.

What success looks like &nbsp;

• Technician utilization rising across the group, measured every week. &nbsp;

• One operating model and one weekly scorecard running in every company, on data that updates itself. &nbsp;

• Measured hours saved through automation, and a pipeline of improvement projects with clear EBITDA impact. &nbsp;

What you will bring &nbsp;

• 3 to 7 years in operations or consulting , with an engineering, supply chain, or manufacturing background, ideally multi- site and large scale . &nbsp;

• Lean or Six Sigma experience , with improvement projects led end to end and a measured before and after. &nbsp;

• Hands-on understanding of technician utilization , absorption, and labor leakage, and how to get leaders to own those numbers. &nbsp;

• Strong Excel and data modeling, P&amp;L literacy, and experience building business cases. &nbsp;

• Working knowledge of APIs, data architecture , and how data moves between systems . You have enough technical proficiency to leverage AI and tech to make our processes more efficient . &nbsp;

• Willingness to work on-site at a partner company most of the week and travel about 50% of the time. &nbsp;

• Sales operations or RevOps , field service trades, a PE-backed business, or an ERP or field service rollout is a plus. &nbsp;

Compensation and benefits &nbsp;

• $100,000 to $125,000 base salary, plus an annual performance bonus.&nbsp;

• Competitive benefits package including healthcare, dental, vision, 401k, etc.&nbsp;
